{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The fee is chargeable only if all four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold, and limb (c) requires a continuous dwell of at least the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the arrival marker. On the driver's own clean trace the longest continuous in-geofence run is 170 seconds (19:00:00 to 19:02:50), 130 seconds short of that minimum. The primary clause therefore does not make this wait sufficient, and the charge can stand only if the separate in-geofence intervals are added together at all.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09107", "EV-TRIP-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's complaint is exactly what the trace records: the driver was outside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius from 19:02:50 to 19:03:50, a 60-second absence during which he reached 179.8 m from the pin, and his own message at 19:02:30 announced that he had to circulate and would return to the same bay. A 170-second hold and a 160-second hold are not one continuous hold; the charge survives only if POL-NS-06(i) lets them be summed, and even then the accumulated 330 seconds clears the 300-second minimum by just 30 seconds (derived shortfall -30 s).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09107", "EV-CHAT-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.excursions",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip record's wait_time_min of 6.2 minutes is not the measure POL-NS-01 limb (c) prescribes. It runs from the arrival marker and includes the 60 seconds during which the vehicle was away from the bay circulating, whereas the clause measures in-geofence dwell from the first qualifying fix. An elapsed six-minute figure taken from the trip record cannot supply the continuity that limb (c) requires and that the trace's 170-second longest run does not show.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09107", "EV-GPS-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own position and the rider's silence are not part of this arithmetic. POL-NS-06 directs the refund to be decided on the dwell computation 'whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages', so the rider's track and the absence of any rider message during the waiting window cannot be used to convert a short in-geofence hold into a chargeable fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09107", "EV-CHAT-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-07 makes driver compensation payable only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it. Because the continuous-dwell limb is not made out on the primary clause and the whole dispute is about whether the two holds may be added, the precondition for the SGD 3.20 compensation figure itemised in the fare breakdown is absent and no driver payment should issue.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09107", "EV-FARE-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The whole of the contested amount sits on the rider: the fare breakdown shows a single SGD 4.00 cancellation fee, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, with no booking or platform fee component to apportion. If the dwell requirement is not satisfied the cancellation-fee line falls away in full under POL-NS-06 and the return to the rider is the entire SGD 4.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09107", "EV-TRIP-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.2,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.2,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute is about the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee on trip TRP-09107, and the fee stands as charged. The money this ruling moves is SGD 3.20 to the driver.\n\nRider — your claim is that the car left the bay during the waiting period, so the two waits should not be added together. That argument is answered on the face of the clause you invoke. The charge is valid only if all four conditions of POL-NS-01 hold, and they do. (a) The trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 19:00:20. (b) The GPS trace puts the driver inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius from 19:00:00 onward, before that event (35 of his 40 fixes qualify). (c) The required dwell is 300 seconds measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix. The trace shows two in-geofence holds — 170 seconds (19:00:00–19:02:50) and 160 seconds (19:03:50–19:06:30) — split by a 60-second circulation in which the driver never went further than 179.76 m from the pin, inside the 300 m leash. POL-NS-06(i) expressly permits these separate intervals to be summed, because a CLOSURE traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09107-01) whose geometry covers the pickup road was active from 18:50 to 19:30, covering the whole waiting period, and holding position was therefore not lawfully possible. 170 + 160 = 330 seconds, which clears the 300-second minimum by 30 seconds. So the two waits do count together. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 19:06:30 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW.\n\nYour remaining points are correct but do not change the outcome, and the ruling has not rested on any of them. Your point that the trip record's 6.2-minute wait_time_min is not the clause's measure is right; the decision uses the 330 seconds of in-geofence dwell, not the elapsed marker-to-cancel figure. Your point that the rider's own position and silence are not part of the arithmetic is also right; POL-NS-06 decides the clock whether or not the rider was present or responsive, and the fee here stands on the clock alone. Your point that a driver payment cannot issue without a fully satisfied POL-NS-01 fails, because with the permitted summation POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full. And because the dwell requirement is met, the SGD 4.00 cancellation-fee line does not fall away, so there is no refund of the contested amount.\n\nDriver — compensation is payable. POL-NS-07 pays 80 percent of the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee, which is SGD 3.20, and the residual SGD 0.80 (4.00 minus 3.20) is retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, and 1 divided by 120 completed trips in 30 days is 0.008, below 0.08. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee: POL-NS-03 does not apply because the driver was inside the arrival radius rather than at a wrong face of the venue; POL-NS-04 does not apply because no rider message appears in the chat log; POL-NS-05 does not fire because at the 19:00:20 arrival marker the driver was stationary inside the geofence, not beyond 300 m and not at or above 15 km/h; and POL-NS-06 leaves the fee intact because the summing rule brings the dwell above the minimum.\n\nOn integrity: the GPS trace is complete (40 fixes, no gaps, 100 percent coverage, zero clock skew against the trip record), the chat log matches the trip record's message count of 3 with contiguous message numbering, and the SGD 4.00 fee equals the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), so there is no POL-NS-08 defect. Every artifact the ruling relies on carries weight 1.0. No escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 is engaged and no clause produces a referral.",
    "amount_sgd_note": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.2,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.2,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.92,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: this dispute is about the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-09107, filed by the rider.\n\nTo the rider. I have not upheld your claim. You are right about the underlying facts: the driver left the marked bay from 19:02:50 to 19:03:50, reaching 179.8 m from the pin, so his two holds inside the geofence were separate — 170 seconds (19:00:00 to 19:02:50) and 160 seconds (19:03:50 to 19:06:30) — and the longest single hold is far short of the 300-second minimum for this LARGE_VENUE pickup. Your argument is that they must not be added together. POL-NS-06(i) says otherwise on these facts: separate in-geofence intervals in a single pickup attempt may be summed where the driver never travelled more than 300 m from the pin AND an admissible traffic advisory made holding position unlawfully impossible. Both conditions hold. The driver's furthest point during the 60-second circulation was 179.8 m, inside the 300 m leash, and LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-09107-01 is a CLOSURE covering the Orchard Central pickup road, active 18:50–19:30, which covers the whole waiting period. The accumulated dwell is therefore 330 seconds against the 300-second minimum — a surplus of 30 seconds. POL-NS-06(ii) means the advisory does not lower the minimum and does not excuse a shortfall on its own, but once the intervals are summed there is no shortfall to excuse. Your own position does not rescue the argument either: your device fixes sit 519 m from the pin (outside the 150 m rider-presence radius), but POL-NS-06 decides the fee 'whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages', and POL-NS-04 cannot apply at all because no message in the chat log was sent by you. The trip record's 6.2-minute wait_time_min, measured from the arrival marker rather than the first fix, is not the clause's measure — but the summed trace dwell still clears the minimum, so nothing turns on it. Finally, the arrival marker was not a false one under POL-NS-05 (at 19:00:20 the driver was inside the 120 m radius, not beyond 300 m and not in motion), and the SGD 4.00 charge reconciles exactly with the fee schedule — the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) is SGD 4.00 — so there is no billing-integrity defect under POL-NS-08(d). Your charge stands.\n\nTo the driver. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full: an arrival event is recorded at 19:00:20; the trace places you inside the 120 m pickup geofence from 19:00:00, before that event; the in-geofence dwell, summed under POL-NS-06(i), is 330 seconds against the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum; and the trip was terminated by you at 19:06:30 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event, after the required dwell had elapsed. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee. Your compensation under POL-NS-07 is 80% of the SGD 4.00 fee, i.e. SGD 3.20. The anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the count threshold of 4, and 1 divided by 120 completed trips in 30 days is 0.008, below the 0.08 rate. Per POL-GEN-03 the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, amount_sgd mirrors your compensation of SGD 3.20, and the rider's charge stands as it presently is.\n\nEvidence and confidence. Every artifact I relied on carries weight_multiplier 1.0 and none is impaired for policy purposes: the GPS trace has 100% coverage, a 10-second cadence, no gap over 120 seconds and a present rider_track; the chat log's three messages match trip_record.chat_message_count with no missing msg_ids and no gap over five minutes across the arrival marker; the fare line reconciles; and there is no clock skew between the arrival event and the nearest fix. No POL-NS-09 trigger is engaged — confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the artifacts do not contradict one another on arrival, dwell or rider presence, there are no repeated disputes between these parties, and the anti-farming check does not trip. No clause produces a referral, so the referrals list is empty."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

